Description: Win+V style clipboard history for Ubuntu
 ClipStack records everything you copy (text, links and images) and shows
 the history in a small popup when you press Super+B. Pick an item to put
 it back on the clipboard and paste it into the window you were using.
 .
 Features: search as you type, pin items so they are kept forever, delete
 single items or clear the history, duplicates move to the top, items from
 password managers are never recorded, and an emoji/symbols tab.
 .
 Works on GNOME, KDE and other desktops, on Wayland and X11.
